# openOODA
File: .github/docs/HOME.oot

A capability-secure systems language.
Every effect needs an unforgeable cap token.
The compiler checks source ahead of time.
Zero ambient authority.

## Caps

Fourteen tokens: filesystem, network, process, GPU, FFI.
A network call takes `&NetCap`. No token, no effect.
Fail closed (`E_CAP`).

## Repos

Ten product repos. Substratum first.

| Repo | Role |
|------|------|
| [openOODA](#openOODA) | Laws, RFCs, practices |
| [oodar](#oodar) | Gen 1 C host |
| [oodac](#oodac) | Compiler |
| [std](#std) | Standard library |
| [ooda](#ooda) | `ooda` driver |
| [packaging](#packaging) | apt, dnf, pacman |
| [opm](#opm) | Package manager |
| [catalog](#catalog) | Public package list |
| [lsp](#lsp) | Language server |
| [mcp](#mcp) | MCP server |

The public site is https://openooda.org.
Org files for GitHub live in this `.github` repo.
